[TestMetricsQLNaNCheck/division - 1]
- description: division
  content: |
    - record: foo
      expr: sum(foo / bar)
  output: |
    2 |   expr: sum(foo / bar)
                          ^^^ This aggregation can return Inf if any series for `bar` evaluates to zero.
  problem:
    reporter: promql/nan
    summary: unsafe division in aggregation
    details: |-
        Division by zero produces `+Inf` in MetricsQL, `NaN` results are treated as missing values.

        Even if only one out of many input series is `Inf`, the entire aggregation result
        becomes `Inf`, making all other valid series irrelevant.
        To avoid this, filter out zero-valued divisor series before division, for example:
        `sum(foo / (bar > 0))`
        See [promql/nan](https://cloudflare.github.io/pint/checks/promql/nan.html) for more details.
    diagnostics:
        - message: This aggregation can return Inf if any series for `bar` evaluates to zero.
          firstcolumn: 11
          lastcolumn: 13
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 2
        last: 2
    severity: 1
    anchor: 0

