[TestMetricsQLRateCheck/deriv_<_1x_default_scrape_interval - 1]
- description: deriv < 1x default scrape interval
  content: |
    - record: foo
      expr: deriv(bar[45s])
  output: |
    2 |   expr: deriv(bar[45s])
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                Duration for `deriv()` must be at least 1 x scrape_interval, `prom` Prometheus server at
                https://simple.example.com is using `1m` scrape_interval.
  problem:
    reporter: promql/rate
    summary: duration too small
    details: |-
        Using [rate](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/metricsql/#rate) and [irate](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/metricsql/#irate) function comes with a few requirements:

        - The metric you calculate (i)rate from must be a counter or a native histogram.
        - The time window of the (i)rate function must have at least 1 sample.

        VictoriaMetrics also uses the last sample before the time window when calculating `rate()`, `irate()` and `deriv()`,
        so the minimal time window you can use is one scrape interval.
        `rate_prometheus()` follows Prometheus semantics and needs at least two scrape intervals.
    diagnostics:
        - message: Duration for `deriv()` must be at least 1 x scrape_interval, `prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com is using `1m` scrape_interval.
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 15
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 2
        last: 2
    severity: 2
    anchor: 0

---

