[TestMetricsQLVectorMatchingCheck/one_to_one_matching - 1]
- description: one to one matching
  content: |
    - record: foo
      expr: foo_with_notfound / bar
  output: |
    2 |   expr: foo_with_notfound / bar
                                    ^^^
                                    The right hand side of the query on `prom` Prometheus server at
                                    https://simple.example.com returns labels: `[instance]`.
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                The left hand side of the query on `prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com
                returns labels: `[instance, notfound]`, which don't match the right hand side labels:
                `[instance]`. This query will never return any results.
  problem:
    reporter: promql/vector_matching
    summary: impossible binary operation
    details: |-
        Trying to match two different time series together will only work if both have the exact same set of labels.
        You can match time series with different labels by using special keywords and follow the rules set by PromQL.
        [Click here](https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/operators/#vector-matching) to read PromQL documentation that explains it.
    diagnostics:
        - message: 'The left hand side of the query on `prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com returns labels: `[instance, notfound]`, which don''t match the right hand side labels: `[instance]`. This query will never return any results.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 17
          kind: 0
        - message: 'The right hand side of the query on `prom` Prometheus server at https://simple.example.com returns labels: `[instance]`.'
          firstcolumn: 21
          lastcolumn: 23
          kind: 1
    lines:
        first: 2
        last: 2
    severity: 2
    anchor: 0

